{"autoMergeRequest":{"authorEmail":null,"commitBody":null,"commitHeadline":null,"mergeMethod":"SQUASH","enabledAt":"2026-11-24T18:58:09Z","enabledBy":{"is_bot":false,"login":"EJRyan89"}},"baseRefName":"main","body":"Closes #2177\n\nEach round's fix brief was written by hand, so what a session was told about the construct's other spellings, a helper's other callers, and the lessons patterns its files meet depended on who wrote it, and the brief's stable part (where to write, the exact local check commands, the pull request rules) lived outside the repository, where no prompt pattern could name it and no test could hold it. implement-change's step 4 now writes the brief from the issue through a tested script: it gathers deterministically, bounds every list and says what each cut left out, and leaves the judgment, the construct and its catalogue, to the session. The stable part moves into a tracked template the script carries into every brief, with a test pinning the exact commands the prompt patterns rely on, as the comment on #2177 asks.\n","changedFiles":12,"files":[{"path":".agents/skills/implement-change/SKILL.md","additions":1,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":".claude/skills/implement-change/SKILL.md","additions":11,"deletions":3,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":".claude/skills/implement-change/references/brief.md","additions":35,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":".claude/skills/implement-change/scripts/fix_brief.py","additions":581,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":".claude/skills/implement-change/scripts/test_fix_brief.py","additions":817,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"docs/implementing-changes.md","additions":5,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"docs/lessons.md","additions":7,"deletions":4,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"skills/ejryan89-skill-core/scripts/implementation_profile.py","additions":9,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"skills/ejryan89-skill-core/scripts/test_implementation_prof